# Template for per-deployment functions config. COMMITTED; the real files are
# NOT.
#
# The source code is deployment agnostic: there is no default region anywhere
# in this repo. For every deploy target, create a local (gitignored) file named
#
#   functions/.env.<projectId>
#
# containing the region that project's functions deploy to. firebase-tools
# loads it at deploy time (function discovery + runtime env). The value MUST
# match that project's Firestore region -- Firestore-triggered functions
# cannot deploy anywhere else -- and must equal the
# VITE_FIREBASE_FUNCTIONS_REGION set in the deploy shell (which is what the
# frontend build reads); keep the two aligned.
#
# Deploys fail loudly if this is missing: functions/src/config/region.ts
# throws at module load, and scripts/deploy.sh refuses to run without the
# shell var.
#
# Illustrations (each line goes in that project's own .env.<projectId>):
#   # functions/.env.tactic-toes-cyphid-dev -- dev Firestore is nam5 (US),
#   # so functions live in us-central1 (also the always-free-tier region):
#   #VITE_FIREBASE_FUNCTIONS_REGION=us-central1
#
#   # functions/.env.team-snek -- production Firestore is australia-southeast1:
#   #VITE_FIREBASE_FUNCTIONS_REGION=australia-southeast1

VITE_FIREBASE_FUNCTIONS_REGION=
